  "body": "- The skill says Wire Contour mounts no tool and naming one is refused; in practice `\"mounts_tool\":true` and omitting the tool gives `\"tool\" is required`.\n- `list_operation_types` shows only top_z, bottom_z and side; the working fields are condition, start, skims, capture, taper_deg, four_axis, tabs, burnout and clearance.\n- The skill still says the wire post does not exist (#533) and that post fails by name; both posts exist now.\n\nDone means: the skill and list_operation_types describe the Wire Contour fields and tool rule as the server takes them (a test compares the field list).\n\nFound in a wire EDM validation run of CamCraft 0.24.0 through the camcraft MCP (2026-11-21), on test parts in `~/Desktop/camcraft/edm-validation/` (EDM-T1 square, EDM-T2 2-axis block, EDM-T3 taper block) and a Sodick owner's own UV part (spikeypineapple, #617). Wire EDM-W025 (0.25 mm), Sodick ALC400G with test conditions.",
